---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Activity from '../components/Activity.astro';

const experience = [
  {
    company: 'JioHotstar',
    logo: '/logos/jiohotstar.png',
    role: 'Senior Software Engineer, Backend',
    dates: '2024 – now',
    bullets: [
      'Architected and own the <b>P0 entitlement read path</b> at <b>~50K RPS</b>, holding P99 SLAs on <b>~20% fewer pods</b>',
      'Re-architected purchase and upgrade flows for <b>~20% revenue growth</b>; team won <b>“Astral Team Award”</b> (2026)',
      'Led the cross-team migration of <b>14M+ JioCinema subscribers</b>',
      'Automated the Disney+ Hotstar → Disney+ plan migration for <b>1K+ plans across 27 countries</b>, cutting ~3 hours of manual launch-day work to <b>under 15 minutes</b> including verification; adopted as the reference for <b>23 of those markets</b>',
      'Helped build the JioCinema entitlement service serving user attributes to core services (Go, Spanner, Redis); team won <b>“Gangstar of the Quarter”</b> (2024)',
      '<b>~20% compute savings</b> from a Graviton + Java 21 migration, packaged as Claude and Codex agent skills for self-serve rollout',
      'Led a <b>SEV-1</b> response at JioCinema when Akamai blocked <b>~200K payment-gateway renewal webhooks</b>; restored <b>~70K renewals within 3 hours</b> by fixing the reconciliation cron, which was calling the wrong status-check API',
      'IPL on-call at <b>30M+ concurrent viewers</b> · LLD/HLD hiring panelist (<b>20+ interviews</b>) · ran Go and Spanner knowledge-sharing sessions that got <b>3 teammates</b> contributing independently',
    ],
  },
  {
    company: 'FamPay',
    logo: '/logos/fampay.png',
    note: '(YC S19)',
    role: 'Software Engineer, Backend',
    dates: '2020 – 2024',
    bullets: [
      'Joined as the <b>second backend engineer</b>; led a team of four on FamCard: <b>5M+ virtual cards</b>, <b>₹10M+ daily transactions</b>, <b>20–30% lower delivery cost</b>',
      'Architected the <b>gift card platform</b> (<b>₹60 Cr+ cumulative GMV</b>) and built recharge and bill-payment products, around <b>60% of monthly revenue</b>',
      '<b>30+ backend interviews</b>; onboarded new engineers and mentored <b>5+ interns and juniors</b> into full-time roles',
    ],
  },
  {
    company: 'Instamojo',
    logo: '/logos/instamojo.png',
    role: 'Software Engineer, Backend',
    dates: '2019 – 2020',
    bullets: [
      'Automated merchant onboarding, cutting KYC resubmissions by <b>~25%</b>',
      'Built reseller product ingestion that onboarded <b>~15K products</b> in its first month; converted from intern to full-time (PPO)',
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base pageType="ProfilePage">
  <section class="hero">
    <img class="avatar" src="/shagun.jpg" alt="Shagun Khemka, Senior Software Engineer at JioHotstar" width="112" height="112" fetchpriority="high" />
    <h1 class="hi">Hey, I'm Shagun Khemka.</h1>
  </section>
  <p class="tag">
    I build backend platforms that <em>stay fast under heavy load</em>, and production AI systems that stay cheap and correct.
  </p>
  <p class="lede">
    Senior Software Engineer at <b>JioHotstar</b>, working on the subscriptions platform.
    Previously <b>FamPay (YC S19)</b> and <b>Instamojo</b>. Based in Mumbai.
  </p>
  <div class="links">
    <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/shagun-khemka/" target="_blank" rel="me noopener">LinkedIn ↗</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/S2606" target="_blank" rel="me noopener">GitHub ↗</a>
    <a href="https://x.com/shagun_p" target="_blank" rel="me noopener">X ↗</a>
  </div>

  <h2 class="sec">Experience</h2>
  {experience.map((e) => (
    <div class="job">
      <div>
        <div class="co">
          <img class="lg" src={e.logo} alt="" width="22" height="22" loading="lazy" />{e.company}{e.note && <small> {e.note}</small>}<span class="ro">{e.role}</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="d">{e.bullets.map((b) => <li set:html={b} />)}</ul>
      </div>
      <div class="dt">{e.dates}</div>
    </div>
  ))}

  <Activity />

  <h2 class="sec">Projects</h2>

  <article class="pj">
    <div class="top">
      <h3>Document extraction platform<span class="st">in production</span></h3>
      <span class="l private">private</span>
    </div>
    <p class="d">An LLM pipeline, built for a logistics ERP software company, that turns scanned, handwritten consignment notes into validated, structured data. I designed, built and run it on my own.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Evals pick the model:</b> every model, prompt or provider change is scored field by field against a labelled golden set before it ships. I evaluated Claude, GPT, Gemini, Qwen, Mistral and Sarvam side by side, and the cheapest models that got every ledger-critical field right (total amount, invoice value and actual weight) went to production.</li>
      <li><b>Phased model rollout:</b> production runs Gemini 3.8 Flash and GPT-6 Luna, switched tenant by tenant from the admin panel with no redeploy. On the latest eval, GPT-6 Luna is <b>8× cheaper and ~45% faster</b> than Gemini Flash, with those ledger-critical fields at <b>100%</b>.</li>
      <li><b>Guardrails and accept policy:</b> GSTIN checksum and state checks, date and total reconciliation, and fuzzy station matching. A document is auto-added only when every mandatory field passes; otherwise it's flagged for human review with the exact fields named.</li>
      <li><b>Gateway, cost and observability:</b> Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, Mistral and Sarvam sit behind one interface, and tenants can bring their own keys. Every call is metered per tenant, and dashboards track cost per document and latency.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tags"><span>Model selection</span><span>Evals</span><span>Structured outputs</span><span>Human-in-the-loop</span><span>LLM cost metering</span></div>
    <p class="stack">Python · Django · Postgres · GPT / Gemini (production) · Claude, Qwen, Mistral, Sarvam (evaluated) · Pulumi · Prometheus + Grafana</p>
  </article>

  <article class="pj">
    <div class="top">
      <h3>ConsumerBuddy<span class="st">private beta</span></h3>
      <a class="l" href="https://consumerbuddy.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">consumerbuddy.in ↗</a>
    </div>
    <p class="d">An AI product that helps Indian consumers draft and file consumer-court complaints without a lawyer. I built and run it end to end.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Vision and tool use:</b> Claude reads uploaded evidence (PDFs and photos) to write court-format annexure descriptions, and uses its web-search tool to find the opposite party's registered address and legal contacts.</li>
      <li><b>Runtime model routing:</b> a different model per task (Sonnet drafts, Haiku handles lookups and vision), configurable per user cohort from the admin panel without a redeploy. Each paid document pins the model plan it was drafted with, so re-renders are reproducible.</li>
      <li><b>Cost and abuse controls:</b> a per-call cost ledger in INR, hourly and daily AI caps per user, and input limits on every AI feature.</li>
      <li><b>LLM observability and legal review:</b> calls, tokens, latency, errors and INR cost tracked per feature, provider and model. Drafts go to a consumer-law advocate for sign-off before public launch.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tags"><span>Multi-model routing</span><span>Vision</span><span>Tool use</span><span>Cost controls</span><span>LLM observability</span></div>
    <p class="stack">Next.js · FastAPI · Postgres · Claude Sonnet + Haiku (production) · GPT, Gemini, Sarvam (integrated) · AWS via Pulumi · Prometheus + Grafana</p>
  </article>


  <p class="more">Open source, education and certifications → <a href="/background/">Background</a></p>

  <aside class="cta" aria-label="Work with me">
    <img class="cta-av" src="/shagun.jpg" alt="" width="56" height="56" loading="lazy" />
    <div>
      <p class="cta-h">Hiring for backend, platform or AI infra?</p>
      <p class="cta-s">I'm open to Lead / Staff roles. Email is the fastest way to reach me.</p>
      <div class="cta-b">
        <a class="btn" href="mailto:shagun.khemka60@gmail.com">Email me</a>
        <a href="https://cal.com/shagun-khemka" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a call ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </aside>
</Base>
